WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
Begin with the approved requirement
and its test-case reference.

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:08.080
The same idempotency key and payload
must return the original transfer.

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:13.160
The test matrix carries that criterion
into the unit and API layers.

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:16.321
The identifiers in this diagram
are authored trace examples.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.680
The AI candidate becomes
a reviewed pull request.

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:23.360
The unit test checks one insertion
through a fake repository.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:27.520
The API test independently
checks the original transfer ID,

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:32.240
one balanced journal, payer balance
ninety thousand, and recipient balance

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:36.561
ten thousand minor units.
A response-status check alone is rejected.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:40.320
The first run pins the fixture
and provider-model revisions.

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:45.280
Execute the deliberate duplicate-posting
variant: one journal is expected,

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:48.720
but two are observed.
JUnit reports a failure.

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:53.240
Retain the assertion, trace
and journal identifiers before cleanup.

00:00:53.312 --> 00:00:57.120
This is a designed challenge,
not a reported banking incident.

00:00:57.340 --> 00:00:59.840
The defect record links that failed run.

00:01:00.133 --> 00:01:05.040
AI proposes duplicate posting as
a hypothesis, with evidence references.

00:01:05.227 --> 00:01:08.720
An engineer confirms the cause
and reviews a production-code repair.

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:11.760
Neither the AI summary
nor the repair process

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:14.640
may turn the original
failed run into a pass.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:19.680
A fresh retest uses a new
run identifier and unchanged

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:23.360
payment expectations.
The corrected build should pass,

00:01:23.373 --> 00:01:25.920
while the deliberately faulty
variant must still fail.

00:01:26.112 --> 00:01:30.920
Link the source change and both results so
the reviewer can inspect the difference.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:35.920
The release pack includes the approved
requirement, test commit, fixture and stub

00:01:35.984 --> 00:01:40.960
revisions, failed run,
reviewed defect, repair and retest.

00:01:41.107 --> 00:01:44.720
Check required coverage and real-provider
evidence before deciding.

00:01:44.853 --> 00:01:48.320
If integration proof is absent,
the pack records that gap;

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:50.880
the diagram does not
grant release approval.
